=============================================================================
PART B -- THE ENGINE IN bin/
=============================================================================

Covered: every file in bin/ -- bin/win-x64/, bin/linux-x64/ and bin/lic/
(together, the "Engine").

The Engine is NOT open source and is NOT covered by Part A. It is supplied
here so that the Example Projects, and projects of your own, can be run
without a separate download.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

  a. Run the Engine to run the Example Projects.

  b. Run the Engine for AyMON projects of your own, for any purpose --
     commercial and production use included -- within the limits of the
     FREE edition, which the Engine enforces by itself when it runs without
     a licence file. The FREE edition does not expire. Its limits are part of
     these terms, not merely a technical measure.

  c. Use the education licence file bin/lic/AyMON.lic only for teaching,
     training, courses and workshops, and for trying AyMON out or developing
     a project before it is put into service -- never for production use.
     The Engine accepts that file only for project directories named
     PRJEDU* or PRJDEV*; that is a technical measure, and the condition is
     this paragraph. (The PRJPER_* examples run on the FREE edition.)

  d. Anything beyond the FREE edition's limits -- more documents,
     connections, devices or users, the licensed features, or the education
     licence's capacity in production -- needs a written licence from
     AKYA Canada Inc.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

  e. Redistribute, publish, mirror, repackage, rent, lend or sublicense the
     Engine, or make it available as part of another product or service.
     Link to this repository instead.

  f. Reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Engine, except to the
     extent that applicable law expressly permits despite this limitation,
     and except as an open-source licence recorded in /NOTICE requires for
     the component it covers.

  g. Work around the Engine's limits or its licence check -- by altering,
     patching or emulating it, or by altering a licence file -- or remove or
     alter any notice in the Engine.

COMPONENT TERMS

  Every AyMON binary in bin/ -- AyXDB, AyDATA, AyPRO, the plug-ins AyPRO_*
  and the engine modules AyLIB_*, the Windows .exe / .dll and the Linux
  executable / lib*.so alike -- is the proprietary software of Senol
  Ercetin, exclusively licensed to AKYA Canada Inc., supplied in binary form
  only, under this Part B. Some of them have third-party open-source code
  compiled in; /NOTICE lists it, and that code's own licence applies to it.

  libssl-3-x64.dll    OpenSSL 3.5.1, Apache License 2.0 -- see /NOTICE.
  libcrypto-3-x64.dll (Windows only; on Linux the Engine uses the system's
                      OpenSSL 3.)

  AyLIB_Python        Loads only beside a 64-bit Python 3.11 that you
                      install yourself (PRJEDU_gauge, PRJEDU_pycall). Python
                      is not supplied here and is used under its own
                      licence.

  bin/lic/AyMON.lic   A signed AKYA licence file. It is data, not software;
                      see paragraph c.

  The plug-in SDK, and the source of some plug-ins, may later be published
  in a repository of their own under an open-source licence. Such a licence
  applies to what is published there; it does not change the terms for the
  binaries in this repository.

PATENTS

  The mechanisms implemented by the Engine are the subject of the patent
  application listed in /PATENTS. No patent licence is granted by Part A or
  Part B beyond the right to RUN the Engine as permitted above.

NO WARRANTY, LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

  The Engine is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind; paragraph 4
  of Part A applies equally to it, and paragraph 5 applies with more force:
  this is industrial control software. To the maximum extent permitted by
  law, neither Senol Ercetin nor AKYA Canada Inc. is liable for any
  indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for loss of
  production, data or profit, arising from the use of the Engine or the
